Z||000014||Fiero5||05-14-2001||09:03 AM||||I think that is the "QMTTAS" (Quantum Mechanics Time Travel Actuator Switch).<P>Here is how it works. Relativity tells us in no uncertain terms that faster than light speed is impossible. Not because of any technical restrictions but simply because it is a fundamental part of the way spacetime is constructed. Apparently Einstein's famous equation "E=mc2" proves this, so who are we to argue. Now here is the ' but' that you knew was coming and it comes in the form of Quantum Mechanics and uses a stock automobile for the experiment. The Fiero was used due to it's plastic body panels which allows for less transient electricity.<P>The EPR experiment. This experiment was originally devised by Einstein as an experiment to 'prove' that the original quantum theory was incorrect. The technology did not exist then to actually carry out the experiment, until now! A Pontiac Fiero, equipped with a special Quantum Mechanics Time Travel "spptd" module, and a switch actuator mounted on the dash panel....<P>Steve<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroSSsignature.jpg"> <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000015||p4n1c||05-14-2001||09:13 AM||||My guess is the cooling fan in the front.  A friend of mine took a household light switch and hooked it up on his Dodge Shadow Turbo.  He would flick the switch and the cooling fan would come on.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International||||reg||1
